LOCATION:The Bell House\, Carroll Gardens-Cobble Hill-Gowanus-Red Hook
DESCRIPTION:As Part of The New York Comedy Festival: In Coda/Switch\, Emmy 
 
award winning comic/bestselling author Moshe Kasher presents 1 hour of stan
 
d up about life as a hearing kid raised in an entirely deaf family & his ye
 
ars spent as an ASL interpreter. With tales of ultra Hasidic Brooklyn\, dru
 
g fueled Oakland & long distance phone sex in the Philippines. Sometimes em
 
otional\, sometimes x-rated\, always funny\, this show's about honoring whe
 
re you came from\, slipping between worlds & getting in where you fit in. I
 
t's also about (mostly) masturbation. Door Time: 6:30pm (front bar opens: 5
 
:30pm). Show Time: 7:30pm. 21 & over w/ valid\, government-issued photo ID.
 
 General Admission standing & seating. *Seating 1st come 1st served & not g
 
uaranteed. Arrive early for best selection. *If you have an accessibility r
 
equest\, email thebellhouse@livenation.com prior. *No outside food/drink. $
 
.25 per each ticket sold for a majority of events at The Bell House benefit
 
s Come Tickets & info: https://www.ticketmaster.com/moshe-kasher-codaswitch
 
